 "video_trailer_thumbnail": null, "display_name": "Echoes", "keywords": ["stereoscopic", "photos", "viewer", "3D", "history"], "long_description": "# Echoes\n\n**Explore history in depth through authentic stereoscopic photography.**\n\nEchoes brings history to life through stereoscopic photographs captured from the mid-1800s and beyond. Stand before real moments from the past and experience them in natural depth, witnessing both major historical events and the everyday lives of the people who lived them.\n\n**What You'll Find**\n\n- Authentic stereoscopic photographs from the mid 1800s and beyond\n- Curated historical albums and collections\n- People, places, events, and everyday life preserved as they were seen\n- True three-dimensional depth captured by original stereo cameras\n\n**Preserving Authentic History**\n\nIn an age increasingly shaped by AI-generated content, preserving authentic historical records has never been more important.\n\nEvery image pair in Echoes is an original stereoscopic photograph presented as captured. No AI reconstruction, alteration, or reinterpretation has been applied.\n\nThese photographs remain direct visual records of the past, preserved through film and glass plates more than a century ago.\n\n**Experience the Presence of the Past**\n\nUnlike traditional photographs, stereoscopic images preserve a genuine sense of depth and presence. Faces, streets, landscapes, and forgotten moments emerge with a realism that can feel surprisingly immediate.\n\nEchoes is a place to explore, reflect, and connect with history through authentic moments preserved in remarkable detail.", "short_description": "Echoes brings history to life through authentic stereoscopic photography from the mid-1800s and beyond. Explore curated historical collections and experience authentic 3D photographs with natural depth, seeing history not as distant facts, but as real moments once lived."}]}, "developer_name": null, "developer_privacy_policy_url": "https://www.ga